# Governed CVE waiver list for the InnBucks cell image scan.
#
# RULES (a waiver without all three is a review failure):
#   * every entry carries: the CVE id, an owner, a one-line reason, and a
#     review-by date — as a comment directly above the id
#   * prefer fixing/upgrading over waiving; a waiver is a scheduled debt,
#     not a dismissal
#   * remove entries at their review date or renew them consciously
#
# The Release workflow scans CRITICAL/HIGH with --ignore-unfixed, so only
# FIXABLE vulnerabilities ever gate the push — a red gate means an upgrade
# exists and should usually just be taken.

#
# The exp: date makes Trivy honour a waiver only until its review date, so an
# expired one trips the gate instead of lingering.

# spring-webmvc 6.2.19: XsltView remote code execution (CVE-2026-47884) and
# Server-Sent Events stream corruption with view rendering (CVE-2026-47890).
# Both CRITICAL, fixed only on Spring Framework 7.0 (7.0.9); 6.2.19 is the last
# 6.2 release, so the real fix is the Spring Boot 4 migration.
# Unreachable here: Fineract serves its API through Jersey. Its one Spring MVC
# controller (fineract-security LoginController) returns JSON. No source file
# uses XsltView, ModelAndView, SseEmitter or ResponseBodyEmitter, and nothing
# configures a ViewResolver or an XSLT stylesheet (grep, 29 Oct 2026).
# Re-check at review: a view, an emitter or an XSLT resource added since
# makes these reachable, and the waiver must go.
# owner: mpofuslim
# review by: 2027-01-31
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2027-01-31
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2027-01-31
